  "notes": "ミスる is formed by adding the verb ending る to the English loanword ミス (miss/mistake). This is a productive pattern in colloquial Japanese where loanwords are turned into godan verbs.\n\nConjugates as a godan verb ending in る:\n- ミスる (present)\n- ミスった (past)\n- ミスらない (negative)\n- ミスって (te-form)\n\nREGISTER:\nCasual/colloquial. In formal contexts, use:\n- {間違|まちが}える: to make a mistake\n- {失敗|しっぱい}する: to fail\n- ミスをする: to make an error (semi-formal)\n\nSIMILAR LOANWORD VERBS:\n- サボる: to skip/slack off (from French \"sabotage\")\n- ダブる: to overlap/repeat (from English \"double\")\n- ハモる: to harmonize (from English \"harmony\")\n\nNOTE:\nVery common among younger speakers and in casual workplace conversation.",
